O2: a customer WAF rule group referenced first by the guidance's web ACL (FAST Channels overlay, guidance v1.4.0)

The guidance creates its CloudFront web ACL in a custom resource and deletes it with the lock token from creation,
so any later UpdateWebACL makes stack deletion fail, and it has no extension point for customer rules. New stack
parameter ExtraWafRuleGroupArn (default empty: no change): the web ACL references that rule group at priority 0,
before every guidance rule, and the custom resource's role may reference rule groups. Changing the rule group's
rules (rotating an origin secret) never touches the web ACL. The ARN is read when the web ACL is created.

diff --git a/source/infrastructure/custom_resources/waf_webacl_lambda/create_waf_webacl.py b/source/infrastructure/custom_resources/waf_webacl_lambda/create_waf_webacl.py
